<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44838" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sostrătus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σώστρατος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Greek proper
			name</i>, esp. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A sculptor</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 34,
				8, 19, § 51 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>An architect of Cnidus</i>, <i>who
				built the tower of Pharos</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 36,
				12, 18, § 83</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>A surgeon</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 4, 3,
				14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7</span></i>
		praef.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
